  "focus_actionability": 0.85,
  "rationale": "The columns collectively centre on one coherent, data-inferable focus: the substantive aspects of the purchase that reviewers actually talk about. Two columns (functional_performance_issue, content_creative_quality) are genuine aspect facets, cleanly split along the functional-vs-creative divide that mirrors the product_category distribution, and each uses categorical value sets that decompose the aspect rather than restating it. product_category is a supporting segmentation dimension that scopes which aspects apply, giving a sound predictor/facet structure rather than a grab-bag or a single restatement. The 'not_present' values enable presence/absence analysis of each aspect. The implied focus is genuinely actionable: an analyst can quantify which aspects dominate per category and drill into performance vs creative complaints. Minor deductions: aspect coverage is not exhaustive (e.g., price/value, shipping, customer service aspects are absent), so the aspect decomposition is somewhat partial, and product_category leans toward context rather than a pure aspect."
}
